  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"Refreshments stay in the designated area so game components remain dry; guests can pause their participation briefly with their table’s agreement.\", \"decision\": \"How should refreshments fit around games?\", \"goal\": \"Help guests find compatible games, understand how to play, and enjoy the evening without avoidable waiting or confusion.\", \"problem\": \"A community room is hosting an evening of board games for adults with different levels of experience. Several tables, a host, willing game teachers, short waiting activities, and a varied collection are available. Guests can decline any game and join a later one. Every game has an agreed latest stopping time before the room closes, and ordinary refreshments and conversation have their own small areas.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nPlayers ask their tables for individual refreshment pauses when needed and return before their next required action. Personal needs can be met at different times without moving drinks or food onto the playing surface.\nThe host announces optional refreshment pauses at broad intervals, and each table takes the next convenient stopping point. A common reminder encourages breaks while allowing games with different structures to pause at suitable moments.\nTables agree short refreshment pauses between rounds, and interested players visit the designated area together. Shared breaks keep the game’s next action clear while giving people a predictable chance to eat or drink."
    }
  ],
